# Tests.AnchorsSimdB — D373: `pminsw`, `pmulhw`, `pmulhuw`, `pavgb` at xmm, against a processor

A NEW metered unit (D373 prediction 3), judged once against an absolute registration measured on its own machine
(`scripts/kernel_ceilings.txt`, `scripts/ku_delta_budget.txt`), so `Tests.AnchorsSimd` keeps its registration.

The block between the markers is GENERATED by `hwprobe/mk_simda_anchors.py --set-b` (`--check --set-b` gates it byte for
byte). The four helpers below restate `Tests.AnchorsSimd`'s, which are private to that module.

LANE. Personal lane, public sources only.
-/
import X86

namespace X86.Tests.SimdB
open X86

/-! ## D373 — four SSE-legacy packed-integer mnemonics against a processor's reading

⚠️ NONE OF THESE HAS A DIFFERENTIAL PARTNER: ACL2 x86isa refuses PMINSW, PMULHW, PMULHUW and PAVGB at every pre-state
(D373, P1).  So the rows below — run by `hwprobe/simda_probe.c` against `simdb_rows.h` on a hosted runner's processor,
derived from the SDM's rules by `hwprobe/mk_simda_rows.py --set-b` — are the only check of this model's numbers for them,
and every row is pinned.  A row agrees exactly as in `Tests.AnchorsSimd`. -/

/-- The six arithmetic flags of an RFLAGS image (CF PF AF ZF SF OF at bits 0 2 4 6 7 11); DF stays clear —
`Tests.Anchors`' `w1bFlags`, restated because that one is private to its module. -/
private def v1aFlags (f : BitVec 64) : Flags :=
  ⟨f.getLsbD 0, f.getLsbD 2, f.getLsbD 4, f.getLsbD 6, f.getLsbD 7, f.getLsbD 11, false⟩

/-- The RFLAGS image of the flags this model keeps, at `flagFields`' positions (`Tests.Anchors`' `b0Rflags`). -/
private def v1aRflags (f : Flags) : BitVec 64 :=
  flagFields.foldl (fun acc r => acc ||| (if r.get f then (1 : BitVec 64) <<< r.bit else 0)) 0

/-- `simdb_ops.S`'s pre-state (the same frame as D335's `simda_ops.S`), at RIP 0x400000 with the m128 source at 0x2000 (16-byte aligned). -/
private def v1aPre (a b : BitVec 128) (f : BitVec 64) : Cpu :=
  ((({ regs := ({} : Regs).set .rbx 0x2000, flags := v1aFlags f, mem := {}, rip := 0x400000,
       oracle := Oracle.zero } : Cpu).setXmm .x0 a).setXmm .x1 b).writeMem128 0x2000 b

private def v1aAgrees (t : Cpu) (n : Nat) (b : BitVec 128) (f : BitVec 64) (w : BitVec 128) : Bool :=
  t.ms.isNone && t.getXmm .x0 == w && t.getXmm .x1 == b && t.readMem128 0x2000 == b
    && (v1aRflags t.flags &&& 0x8d5) == (f &&& 0x8d5) && t.rip == 0x400000 + BitVec.ofNat 64 n

